license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/MuhammadAhmadZia/Inline-Decision-Budgets-for-E-Commerce-Web-Attack-Detection
abstract: >-
  Evaluation code and results for a study of machine-learning web attack detectors for
  e-commerce under inline constraints: matched false-positive rates of 1 percent and 0.1
  percent, three split protocols controlling duplicate leakage, repeated splits, and
  serving cost measured as both a hardware-independent work proxy and single-request
  latency on the CSIC 2010 dataset.
keywords:
  - web attack detection
  - e-commerce security
  - operating point
  - data leakage
  - gradient boosted trees
  - inference cost
  - green machine learning
